findings.body:
The comment says the cached permission allows access "to prove this is not checked", but the map value is `false`. `checkPermission` treats a scope as granted only when `scopeMap[scope]` is true (service.go:558). Without the denial cache, the flow would go like this:
- the cached perms deny the request;
- `checkInheritedPermissions` finds no folders, because `fakeStore.ListFolders` returns nil;
- the DB fallback gets empty `userPermissions` from `fakeStore`.

The result is still `Allowed: false`, so the test does not exercise the denial cache. Set the value to `true` (and ideally assert that `fakeStore.calls == 0`).
